HADWIGER-NELSON (A=R^2, connection=unit circle, Fourier=Bessel J0):
  lambda_max=J0(0)=1, lambda_min=min J0 = -0.4028 (at 2pi|xi|~3.83, 1st min)
  spectral (Hoffman) bound: chi_m >= 1 - lmax/lmin = 3.483 => chi_m >= 4
  (sharper LP/combinatorial: chi>=5 de Grey; the spectral bound is the SAME method, looser.)

LRC as a DISTANCE CAYLEY GRAPH Cay(Z_m, D) (D=speed differences):
  D=[1, 2, 3] mod 7 [AP n=4 (mod 7)]: lambda_max=6.00, lambda_min=-1.00, chi >= 1-lmax/lmin = 7.00
  D=[1, 3, 4] mod 7 [non-AP]: lambda_max=6.00, lambda_min=-2.69, chi >= 1-lmax/lmin = 3.23
  D=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5] mod 11 [AP n=6 (mod 11)]: lambda_max=10.00, lambda_min=-1.00, chi >= 1-lmax/lmin = 11.00

SHARED KEY: chi >= 1 - lambda_max/lambda_min with lambda = Fourier transform of the
connection set -- arc/cosine-sum for LRC, Bessel J0 for the plane. The NEGATIVITY of
the connection-set Fourier transform (sinc<0 / J0<0) drives the chromatic lower bound.
LRC's covering-depth Poisson formula (HYP-2154) and HN's measurable-chromatic LP bound
are the SAME Delsarte/Fourier method on different groups (Z/R-circle vs R^2).
